  "reason": "The strongest evidence so far is that scVI multiprofile RNA models substantially outperform single-profile RNA baselines, with avgpool and transformer aggregation nearly tied. It remains unclear whether this gain is mainly due to multiprofile aggregation or to the scVI representation. config_002 tests PCA multiprofile with avgpool, a one-factor change from config_005 in RNA encoder, so it directly isolates whether multiprofile aggregation helps a simpler RNA representation. This is the best next experiment because it reduces uncertainty about a key design choice before adding image or fusion complexity."
